# Requests from the worksheets, for the IntelliJ HTTP client. Start the service first: scala-cli run .

@host = http://localhost:8080

### Step 0: hello
GET {{host}}/api/hello?name=Berlin

### Step 1: create a link with an alias (201, then 409 when the alias is taken)
POST {{host}}/api/links
Content-Type: application/json

{"url": "https://scala-lang.org", "alias": "scala"}

### Step 1: get a link (404 for an unknown code)
GET {{host}}/api/links/scala

### Step 1: follow a short link (302, the URL in the Location header)
# @no-redirect
GET {{host}}/scala

### Step 2: a flaky preview service: succeeds after retries
POST {{host}}/api/links
Content-Type: application/json

{"url": "https://flaky.example.com"}

### Step 2: a slow title: about 1 s, no title
POST {{host}}/api/links
Content-Type: application/json

{"url": "https://slow.example.com"}

### Step 2: the safety check is down: 503
POST {{host}}/api/links
Content-Type: application/json

{"url": "https://down.example.com"}

### Step 3: import many URLs, at most 10 per second and 4 at a time: one result per URL, in order
POST {{host}}/api/links/import
Content-Type: application/json

{"urls": ["https://scala-lang.org", "nope", "https://lag1.example.com", "https://lag2.example.com"]}

### Step 3: a slow title: the link is created without one
POST {{host}}/api/links
Content-Type: application/json

{"url": "https://slow2.example.com", "alias": "slow"}

### Step 3: a few seconds later, the title refresher has filled it in
GET {{host}}/api/links/slow

### Step 5: the analytics report
GET {{host}}/api/links/scala/report

### Metrics in Prometheus format
GET {{host}}/metrics
